<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 October, from 202 BCE to 1987.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hannibal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/202-bce">202 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,227 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scipio defeats Hannibal at Zama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Publius Cornelius Scipio defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> near Zama in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>; 19 October is the traditional date. The victory ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> dominant in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1216">1216 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">810 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King John dies at Newark Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> died of dysentery at Newark during a civil war with his barons and a French invasion. His nine-year-old son became Henry III, and his regents reissued <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a> to win back support.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1386">1386 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">640 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Heidelberg University holds its first lecture</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after a Pontifical High Mass established it, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-university">Heidelberg University</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-i-elector-palatine">Rupert I, Elector Palatine</a>, held its first lecture, making it the oldest university in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. By March 1390 it had 185 students.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg-university">Heidelberg University</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1453">1453 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">573 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bordeaux falls to the French, ending the Hundred Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three months after the English defeat at Castillon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bordeaux">Bordeaux</a> surrendered to the French, ending three centuries of English rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>. No more hostilities followed, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a> was over.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-castillon">Battle of Castillon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1466">1466 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">560 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Second Peace of Thorn ends the Thirteen Years' War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Polish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-iv-jagiellon">Casimir IV Jagiellon</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> made peace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torun">Toruń</a>, ending the longest of the Polish–Teutonic Wars. Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, with Danzig and Marienburg, passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>; the Order kept the rest as a Polish fief.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466">Thirteen Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cornwallis's army surrenders at Yorktown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged by American and French forces, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis">Lord Cornwallis</a>'s army of about 8,000 surrendered at Yorktown, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>. The defeat effectively ended major fighting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1813">1813 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon retreats after defeat at Leipzig</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig">Battle of the Nations</a> ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s army in retreat from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>, its rearguard trapped when a bridge was blown too early. He lost control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> within months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1987">1987 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">39 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Black Monday: stock markets crash worldwide</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 508 points, or 22.6 per cent, its largest one-day percentage fall. Markets crashed worldwide, though the wider economy recovered far faster than after 1929.</p></div></li></ol>
